corporate-development plugin

This plugin is a port of the `corporate-development` plugin, version
0.18.0, in a private repository of ai-advanced-futures
(plugins/corporate-development/). Luis F. Amadeo wrote it. It is under
the MIT license. This plugin takes the whole plugin from it, with these
changes:

  - It removes the parts for a mission runner of the source repository:
    the mode check, the `automated` field, the `pipeline_result.json`
    handoff, and the text about them.
  - It removes the plugin adapter (the package `corporate_development/plugins`,
    `operational_dd/plugin_integrator.py`, and their test).
  - It removes the slide generation text and the other plugin names that
    this marketplace does not have.
  - It moves each skill to `skills/<group>-<name>/SKILL.md`, and gives each
    agent and each command the frontmatter that Claude Code needs.
  - The commands ask the person. The agents ask nothing. An agent that needs
    an answer writes a questions file, and the command asks.
  - It adds `uv` script headers to the two scripts, a changelog, and the
    file `docs/pipeline-inputs.md`.
  - It moves the tests of the folder `tests/integration` to `tests/unit/flows`.
  - It rewrites the README and the architecture decision record.

